Saturate the page bitmap size in SplashOutputDev::startPage().

A huge MediaBox (times the DPI) gives page sizes beyond the int range, and
static_cast<int>(width + 0.5) is undefined (UBSan: "SplashOutputDev.cc:1326:30:
runtime error: 7.92889e+13 is outside the range of representable values of type
'int'"). Saturate to [1, INT_MAX]; the SplashBitmap allocation then fails and
startPage() falls back to its existing 1x1 bitmap.

No regression test: the conversion is undefined, but no host behaves
differently with the fix. x86-64 gives INT_MIN, which the old "w <= 0" check
turned into a 1-pixel bitmap; wasm32 saturates to INT_MAX, the value this
patch now returns, and the SplashBitmap allocation fails softly either way
("Bogus memory allocation size"). The repro runs without a fault in the
unfixed wasm32 builds of all four fuzz targets; a native ASan+UBSan build
reports only the conversion above (poppler-pdf, poppler-page_search).

Not fixed upstream as of 9182fd5.
Upstream: open umbrella issue poppler/poppler#1764 (by LingMaple, 2026-07-20); open MR !2413 (by rogo1337, 2026-10-24) fixes the same overflow class in SplashOutputDev::beginType3Char, not startPage.

diff --git a/poppler/SplashOutputDev.cc b/poppler/SplashOutputDev.cc
index 357b3f5e2..7ff86a37c 100644
--- a/poppler/SplashOutputDev.cc
+++ b/poppler/SplashOutputDev.cc
@@ -1319,14 +1319,21 @@ void SplashOutputDev::startPage(int /*pageNum*/, GfxState *state, XRef *xrefA)
     xref = xrefA;
     if (state) {
         setupScreenParams(state->getHDPI(), state->getVDPI());
-        w = static_cast<int>(state->getPageWidth() + 0.5);
-        if (w <= 0) {
-            w = 1;
-        }
-        h = static_cast<int>(state->getPageHeight() + 0.5);
-        if (h <= 0) {
-            h = 1;
-        }
+        // page sizes in device space can exceed the int range (huge
+        // MediaBox times DPI); saturate instead of an undefined cast,
+        // the bitmap allocation below then falls back to 1x1
+        const auto toBitmapDim = [](double v) -> int {
+            v += 0.5;
+            if (!(v >= 1)) {
+                return 1;
+            }
+            if (v >= static_cast<double>(INT_MAX)) {
+                return INT_MAX;
+            }
+            return static_cast<int>(v);
+        };
+        w = toBitmapDim(state->getPageWidth());
+        h = toBitmapDim(state->getPageHeight());
     } else {
         w = h = 1;
     }
